Package: ChIPBindVis
Type: Package
Title: ChIP-seq Signal and Peak Visualization at Gene Promoters
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person(given = "Changhao",
                  family = "Kan",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "kch_ynu@163.com")
Description: Visualizes ChIP-seq signal and called peaks around a selected
    gene and across genes with promoter-associated peaks. Given a bigWig
    signal file and a narrowPeak (or broadPeak) file, produces (A) a Gviz
    genome-browser track centered on the selected gene's TSS and (B) a
    strand-aware EnrichedHeatmap across gene-level TSSs. The query gene is
    highlighted only when a promoter-associated peak is detected within the
    configured annotation window. Supports human (hg38, hg19) and mouse
    (mm10, mm39) reference assemblies. Annotation packages for each genome
    are loaded on demand.
